<title>PHILIPPINES: Isuzu Philippines says triples market share.</title>
<headline>Isuzu Philippines says triples market share.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Isuzu Philippines Corp said on Thursday its market share had tripled to about 13 percent of the local commercial vehicle market in the first half of the year.</p>
<p>Isuzu recently launched two light commercial vehicle models to cater to the growing number of small and medium enterprises.</p>
<p>Isuzu used to earlier concentrate on assembling trucks and buses.</p>
<p>Isuzu Philippines is a joint venture of Isuzu Motors Ltd, Mitsubishi Corp, Ayala Corp and Rizal Commercial Banking Corp. The two Japanese companies own 35 percent each, while the two Filipino companies, 15 percent each.</p>
<p>-- Manila Newsroom (63 2) 841-8938 Fax 817-6267</p>
